Fix the GCC target pragma when AESCE is compiled without -march=...+crypto on
the command line.

Upstream's `pragma GCC target("+crypto")` is the correct syntax for AArch64
GCC but is silently a no-op on AArch32 GCC — the AES intrinsics in arm_neon.h
are still flagged with mismatched target attributes and `always_inline` calls
fail with "target specific option mismatch". On AArch32 GCC the working
incantation is `pragma GCC target("fpu=crypto-neon-fp-armv8")`.

This matters for downstream builds (e.g. Buildroot/Nerves on rpi3) that ship
a stock toolchain whose default -march does not include +crypto, relying on
the fallback pragma block to enable the intrinsics for the AESCE TU.

--- a/aesce.c
+++ b/aesce.c
@@ -96,7 +96,11 @@
 #       define MBEDTLS_POP_TARGET_PRAGMA
 #   elif defined(__GNUC__)
 #       pragma GCC push_options
+#       if defined(__aarch64__)
 #       pragma GCC target ("+crypto")
+#       else
+#       pragma GCC target ("fpu=crypto-neon-fp-armv8")
+#       endif
 #       define MBEDTLS_POP_TARGET_PRAGMA
 #   elif defined(_MSC_VER)
 #       error "Required feature(__ARM_FEATURE_AES) is not enabled."
